' COIL - you against the computer (NovaBASIC)›' A title screen, then the game. The joystick steers your snake, the›' computer plays the other one. Same rules for both: wall or any snake›' body = death, apple = grow. Fire = play again, START = title screen.›' Music plays on the title screen only (see PROC PlayMusic).››DIM WALL(8) BYTE = $00,$4D,$CF,$CF,$00,$53,$F3,$F3›DIM BODY(8) BYTE = $00,$14,$55,$55,$57,$5D,$14,$00›DIM APPLE(8) BYTE = $00,$28,$8A,$8A,$AA,$AA,$28,$00›DIM CPUBODY(8) BYTE = $00,$3C,$FF,$FF,$FD,$F7,$3C,$00›' tails: the oldest segment of each snake›DIM TAILP(8) BYTE = $00,$00,$14,$14,$14,$1C,$00,$00›DIM TAILC(8) BYTE = $00,$00,$3C,$3C,$3C,$34,$00,$00›' heads: the newest segment of each snake (the eye is a gap in the pattern)›DIM HEADP(8) BYTE = $00,$14,$45,$55,$55,$5D,$14,$00›DIM HEADC(8) BYTE = $00,$3C,$CF,$FF,$FF,$F7,$3C,$00›' sound effects: pairs of (pitch, control), one pair per frame.›' pitch: bigger number = lower note (120 = middle C, 60 = C5, 40 = G5)›' control: $A = pure tone, second digit = volume›' HAPPY: two rising notes, C5 then G5 (you ate an apple)›DIM HAPPY(24) BYTE = 60,$AA, 60,$AA, 60,$A8, 60,$A4,›  40,$AB, 40,$AB, 40,$AA, 40,$A8, 40,$A6, 40,$A4, 40,$A2, 40,$A1›' SAD: two falling notes, G4 then E-flat 4, fading out (CPU ate an apple)›DIM SAD(26) BYTE = 80,$A9, 80,$A9, 80,$A8, 80,$A6, 80,$A3,›  101,$A9, 101,$A9, 101,$A8, 101,$A7, 101,$A6, 101,$A4, 101,$A2, 101,$A1›DIM CRASH(12) BYTE = 100,$8F, 130,$8D, 160,$8B, 190,$88, 220,$85, 250,$82››' --- title screen›' 4 animation frames of the logo tile (8 rows each): %10 = letter colour›' (colour 1), %01 = a golden dot (colour 0) moving diagonally›DIM SHIMMER(32) BYTE = %01101010,%10011010,%10100110,%10101001,›  %01101010,%10011010,%10100110,%10101001,›  %10011010,%10100110,%10101001,%01101010,›  %10011010,%10100110,%10101001,%01101010,›  %10100110,%10101001,%01101010,%10011010,›  %10100110,%10101001,%01101010,%10011010,›  %10101001,%01101010,%10011010,%10100110,›  %10101001,%01101010,%10011010,%10100110›' work buffer for the current frame›DIM CURR_TILE(8) BYTE››' the logo as text: 5 rows of 24 characters, 1 = a tile of the logo›DIM LOGO(120) BYTE = ".1111...1111..1111.11...",›  "11..11.11..11..11..11...",›  "11.....11..11..11..11...",›  "11..11.11..11..11..11...",›  ".1111...1111..1111.11111"›DIM FANFARE(12) BYTE = 60,$AA, 50,$AA, 40,$AA, 30,$AB, 25,$AC, 20,$AF››' --- title music: 3 voices (channels 0-2), channel 3 stays free for SFX›' A DIM size is 2 x the number of (note, duration) pairs. Every part›' loops by itself, so the short parts accompany the long melody:›'   LEAD 256 ticks = 16 bars, BASS 128 ticks (2 times), HATS 16 (16 times)›' TEMPO 3 = 1 tick = 3 frames (4 ticks per beat = 250 BPM)›DIM LEAD(112) BYTE = 13,4, 17,4, 20,4, 17,4, 13,4, 20,4, 25,6, 0,2,›  22,4, 18,4, 22,4, 20,4, 17,8, 0,8,›  18,4, 22,4, 20,4, 18,4, 17,4, 20,4, 18,4, 17,4,›  15,4, 18,4, 20,4, 22,4, 20,12, 0,4,›  25,4, 24,4, 22,4, 20,4, 17,4, 20,4, 25,6, 0,2,›  22,4, 20,4, 18,4, 17,4, 20,8, 0,8,›  18,4, 20,4, 22,4, 25,4, 24,4, 22,4, 20,4, 18,4,›  15,4, 17,4, 18,4, 20,4, 25,12, 0,4›' bass: root and fifth, chords C, Am, F, G (2 bars each)›DIM BASS(64) BYTE = 1,6, 0,2, 8,6, 0,2,   1,6, 0,2, 8,6, 0,2,›  10,6, 0,2, 5,6, 0,2,   10,6, 0,2, 5,6, 0,2,›  6,6, 0,2, 1,6, 0,2,   6,6, 0,2, 1,6, 0,2,›  8,6, 0,2, 3,6, 0,2,   8,6, 0,2, 3,6, 0,2›' hi-hat: 4 hits per bar›DIM HATS(16) BYTE = 45,1, 0,3, 45,1, 0,3, 45,1, 0,3, 45,1, 0,3››' tile on the map for each snake: 2 = player, 132 = computer›' (tile 4 + 128 draws the 11-pixels in colour 3)›DIM TILEOF(2) = 2, 132›' tail tile for each snake: 5 = player, 134 = computer (tile 6 + 128)›DIM TAILOF(2) = 5, 134›' head tile for each snake: 7 = player, 140 = computer (tile 12 + 128)›DIM HEADOF(2) = 7, 140›DIM STARTX(2) = 10, 29›DIM STARTY(2) = 8, 16›DIM STARTD(2) = 1, -1››' snake data, index 0 = player, 1 = computer›DIM HX(2), HY(2), DX(2), DY(2), HD(2), TL(2), LIVE(2), PTS(2)›' ring buffers of body positions: snake S uses S * 512 + index›DIM SNX(1024) BYTE›DIM SNY(1024) BYTE››HI = 0››SCREEN 12›SETCOLOR 4, 0, 0›SETCOLOR 0, 1, 12›SETCOLOR 1, 9, 14›SETCOLOR 2, 1, 8›SETCOLOR 3, 2, 8›CHARDEF 1, WALL›CHARDEF 2, BODY›CHARDEF 3, APPLE›CHARDEF 4, CPUBODY›CHARDEF 5, TAILP›CHARDEF 6, TAILC›CHARDEF 7, HEADP›CHARDEF 12, HEADC›' NOTE: a tile number is also the screen code of a text character (tiles›' 1-15 = the characters ! to /). TEXT must not print a character that has›' a tile. Tiles in use: 1-7, 10-12 and 15, so texts must not contain quote,›' hash, dollar, percent, ampersand, apostrophe, star, plus, comma or slash.›' Tiles 8 and 9 stay free: they are the parentheses of the (C) line.››DO›  Title›  GOTITLE = 0›  WHILE GOTITLE = 0›    Round›    REPEAT›      FRAME›      BTN = STRIG(0)›      STRT = CONSOL() AND 1›    UNTIL BTN <> 0 OR STRT <> 0›    IF STRT <> 0 THEN GOTITLE = 1›  WEND›LOOP››' --- one round: play until a snake dies, then the GAME OVER banner›PROC Round›  NewGame›  WHILE LIVE(0) = 1 AND LIVE(1) = 1›    FOR T = 1 TO DELAY›      GetInput›      FRAME›    NEXT›    ThinkAI›    S = 0 : MoveSnake›    S = 1 : MoveSnake›  WEND›  SFX 3, CRASH›  BannerOn›  IF LIVE(0) = 0 AND LIVE(1) = 0›    TEXT 18, 12, "DRAW"›  ELSEIF LIVE(0) = 0›    TEXT 16, 12, "YOU LOSE"›  ELSE›    TEXT 17, 12, "YOU WIN"›  ENDIF›  TEXT 11, 13, "FIRE = PLAY AGAIN"›  TEXT 13, 14, "START = TITLE"›  PAUSE 50›ENDPROC››PROC NewGame›  BannerOff›  MAPFILL 0›  FOR X = 0 TO 39 : SETTILE X, 1, 1 : SETTILE X, 23, 1 : NEXT›  FOR Y = 1 TO 23 : SETTILE 0, Y, 1 : SETTILE 39, Y, 1 : NEXT›  TEXT 0, 0, "SCORE"›  TEXT 14, 0, "CPU"›  TEXT 28, 0, "HI"›  DELAY = 8›  MX = 1 : MY = 0›  FOR S = 0 TO 1›    B = S * 512›    HX(S) = STARTX(S) : HY(S) = STARTY(S)›    DX(S) = STARTD(S) : DY(S) = 0›    TL(S) = 0 : HD(S) = 2›    LIVE(S) = 1 : PTS(S) = 0›    FOR I = 0 TO 2›      XX = STARTX(S) - (2 - I) * STARTD(S)›      SNX(B + I) = XX : SNY(B + I) = STARTY(S)›      SETTILE XX, STARTY(S), TILEOF(S)›    NEXT›    SETTILE SNX(B), SNY(B), TAILOF(S)›    SETTILE HX(S), HY(S), HEADOF(S)›  NEXT›  PlaceFood›  ShowScore›ENDPROC››' --- the player: joystick, turning back on yourself is not allowed›PROC GetInput›  JX = JOYX(0) : JY = JOYY(0)›  IF JX <> 0 AND MX = 0›    DX(0) = JX : DY(0) = 0›  ELSEIF JY <> 0 AND MY = 0›    DX(0) = 0 : DY(0) = JY›  ENDIF›ENDPROC››' --- the computer (snake 1)›' 1. head for the apple (along the longer distance first)›' 2. if that way is blocked, turn to the side where it is free›' 3. nothing free at all: go straight on (and crash)›PROC ThinkAI›  FOUND = 0›  AX = SGN(FX - HX(1)) : AY = SGN(FY - HY(1))›  IF ABS(FX - HX(1)) >= ABS(FY - HY(1))›    CX = AX : CY = 0 : TryDir›    CX = 0 : CY = AY : TryDir›  ELSE›    CX = 0 : CY = AY : TryDir›    CX = AX : CY = 0 : TryDir›  ENDIF›  IF RAND(2) = 0›    CX = DY(1) : CY = -DX(1) : TryDir›    CX = -DY(1) : CY = DX(1) : TryDir›  ELSE›    CX = -DY(1) : CY = DX(1) : TryDir›    CX = DY(1) : CY = -DX(1) : TryDir›  ENDIF›  CX = DX(1) : CY = DY(1) : TryDir›ENDPROC››' tries direction (CX, CY) for the computer: takes it if the field is›' empty or an apple, and only if no earlier try was successful›PROC TryDir›  IF FOUND = 1 THEN RETURN›  IF CX = 0 AND CY = 0 THEN RETURN›  K = GETTILE(HX(1) + CX, HY(1) + CY)›  IF K = 0 OR K = 3›    DX(1) = CX : DY(1) = CY›    FOUND = 1›  ENDIF›ENDPROC››' --- one step of snake S (the same code for both snakes)›PROC MoveSnake›  IF S = 0 THEN MX = DX(0) : MY = DY(0)›  B = S * 512›  NX = HX(S) + DX(S) : NY = HY(S) + DY(S)›  K = GETTILE(NX, NY)›  IF K <> 3›    ' no apple: the tail moves on›    SETTILE SNX(B + TL(S)), SNY(B + TL(S)), 0›    TL(S) = (TL(S) + 1) AND 511›    SETTILE SNX(B + TL(S)), SNY(B + TL(S)), TAILOF(S)›    K = GETTILE(NX, NY)›  ENDIF›  IF K <> 0 AND K <> 3 THEN LIVE(S) = 0 : RETURN›  SETTILE HX(S), HY(S), TILEOF(S)›  HX(S) = NX : HY(S) = NY›  HD(S) = (HD(S) + 1) AND 511›  SNX(B + HD(S)) = NX : SNY(B + HD(S)) = NY›  SETTILE NX, NY, HEADOF(S)›  IF K = 3›    PTS(S) = PTS(S) + 1›    IF PTS(0) > HI THEN HI = PTS(0)›    IF S = 0 THEN SFX 3, HAPPY ELSE SFX 3, SAD›    IF (PTS(0) + PTS(1)) MOD 4 = 0 AND DELAY > 3 THEN DELAY = DELAY - 1›    PlaceFood›    ShowScore›  ENDIF›ENDPROC››PROC PlaceFood›  REPEAT›    FX = 1 + RAND(38)›    FY = 2 + RAND(21)›  UNTIL GETTILE(FX, FY) = 0›  SETTILE FX, FY, 3›ENDPROC››PROC ShowScore›  NROW = 0›  V = PTS(0) : NCOL = 6 : DrawNum›  V = PTS(1) : NCOL = 18 : DrawNum›  V = HI : NCOL = 31 : DrawNum›ENDPROC››PROC DrawNum›  FOR P = 3 TO 0 STEP -1›    SETTILE NCOL + P, NROW, 16 + V MOD 10›    V = V / 10›  NEXT›ENDPROC››' Sets the mode of map row ROWN: RMODE = 2 (text) or 4 (tiles).›' The instruction of row r sits at $9403 + 3 * r; $40 = "load address".›PROC RowMode›  POKE $9403 + 3 * ROWN, $40 + RMODE›ENDPROC››' GAME OVER banner: rows 12-14 become text lines. The tiles in these rows›' are cleared first, as mode 2 would show them as odd characters.›PROC BannerOn›  FOR R = 12 TO 14›    FOR X = 0 TO 39 : SETTILE X, R, 0 : NEXT›    ROWN = R : RMODE = 2 : RowMode›  NEXT›ENDPROC››' back to normal tile rows (harmless when they already are)›PROC BannerOff›  FOR R = 12 TO 14›    ROWN = R : RMODE = 4 : RowMode›  NEXT›ENDPROC››' Sets the mode of map rows FR to LR (RMODE = 2 text, 4 tiles).›PROC RowsMode›  FOR R = FR TO LR›    ROWN = R : RowMode›  NEXT›ENDPROC››' title screen: row 0 and the banner rows are tiles, rows 16-20 are text›PROC TitleModes›  RMODE = 4›  FR = 0 : LR = 0 : RowsMode›  FR = 12 : LR = 14 : RowsMode›  RMODE = 2›  FR = 16 : LR = 20 : RowsMode›ENDPROC››' game: rows 16-20 are tiles again, row 0 is the text line of the score›PROC GameModes›  RMODE = 4›  FR = 16 : LR = 20 : RowsMode›  RMODE = 2›  FR = 0 : LR = 0 : RowsMode›ENDPROC››' --- the title screen: logo with shimmer, blinking text, fire starts›PROC Title›  MAPFILL 0›  TitleModes›  TEXT 10, 16, "THE DUEL: YOU VS CPU"›  TEXT 10, 17, "PRESS FIRE TO START"›  TEXT 13, 18, "HI-SCORE"›  NROW = 18 : NCOL = 22 : V = HI : DrawNum›  TEXT 9, 19, "(C) 2026 KAMIL SOBCZAK"›  TEXT 5, 20, "CODED WITH HELP FROM CLAUDE.AI"›  FRAME_ANIM = 0 : ShimmerFrame›  DrawLogo›  HP = 99 : LN = 3 : RETR = 0 : LONGEST = 30 : SNK = 0›  TitleApple›  PlayMusic›  TIMER = 0 : BLINK = 1 : SPEED_ANIM = 0›  DO›    TIMER = TIMER + 1›    IF TIMER >= 25›      TIMER = 0›      BLINK = 1 - BLINK›      IF BLINK = 1›        TEXT 10, 17, "PRESS FIRE TO START"›      ELSE›        TEXT 10, 17, "                   "›      ENDIF›    ENDIF›    SPEED_ANIM = SPEED_ANIM + 1›    IF SPEED_ANIM >= 3›      SPEED_ANIM = 0›      FRAME_ANIM = (FRAME_ANIM + 1) MOD 4›      ShimmerFrame›    ENDIF›    SNK = SNK + 1›    IF SNK >= 4›      SNK = 0›      SnakeStep›    ENDIF›    FRAME›    IF STRIG(0) THEN EXIT›  LOOP›  MSTOP›  SFX 3, FANFARE›  PAUSE 25›  MAPFILL 0›  GameModes›ENDPROC››' copies the 8 bytes of the current frame and redefines the logo tile 15›PROC ShimmerFrame›  FOR B = 0 TO 7›    CURR_TILE(B) = SHIMMER(FRAME_ANIM * 8 + B)›  NEXT›  CHARDEF 15, CURR_TILE›ENDPROC››PROC DrawLogo›  FOR Y = 0 TO 4›    FOR X = 0 TO 23›      IF LOGO(Y * 24 + X) = ASC("1") THEN SETTILE 8 + X, 6 + Y, 15›    NEXT›  NEXT›ENDPROC››' --- the snake on the title screen›' The frame is a closed loop of 116 fields, numbered clockwise from the›' top-left corner: 0-37 top row, 38-57 right side, 58-95 bottom row,›' 96-115 left side. A snake is just a head field HP and a length LN: the›' body lies on the fields behind the head, so no buffers are needed.›' Fields in rows 16-20 are hidden behind the text rows: nothing is drawn.›PROC PathXY›  IF PP < 38›    PX = 1 + PP : PY = 1›  ELSEIF PP < 58›    PX = 38 : PY = PP - 36›  ELSEIF PP < 96›    PX = 96 - PP : PY = 22›  ELSE›    PX = 1 : PY = 117 - PP›  ENDIF›ENDPROC››' draws tile TT on field PP (unless it is hidden behind the text rows)›PROC DrawCell›  PathXY›  IF PY < 16 OR PY > 20 THEN SETTILE PX, PY, TT›ENDPROC››' a new apple 8 to 32 fields ahead of the head, never behind the text rows›PROC TitleApple›  REPEAT›    AP = (HP + 8 + RAND(25)) MOD 116›    PP = AP : PathXY›  UNTIL PY < 16 OR PY > 20›  TT = 3 : DrawCell›ENDPROC››' one step: the snake walks on and grows by the apples. Once it is›' LONGEST long and its head gets behind the text rows, the head stops and›' the tail walks in (RETR = 1) until only the head is left. Then a short›' snake starts again behind the left text rows.›PROC SnakeStep›  TP = (HP + 117 - LN) MOD 116›  IF RETR = 1›    PP = TP : TT = 0 : DrawCell›    LN = LN - 1›    IF LN <= 1›      LN = 3 : HP = 99 : RETR = 0›    ELSE›      PP = (TP + 1) MOD 116 : TT = 5 : DrawCell›    ENDIF›    RETURN›  ENDIF›  NP = (HP + 1) MOD 116›  PP = HP : TT = 2 : DrawCell›  IF NP = AP›    LN = LN + 1›    TitleApple›  ELSE›    PP = TP : TT = 0 : DrawCell›    PP = (TP + 1) MOD 116 : TT = 5 : DrawCell›  ENDIF›  HP = NP›  PP = HP : TT = 7 : DrawCell›  IF LN >= LONGEST›    PathXY›    IF PY >= 16 AND PY <= 20 THEN RETR = 1›  ENDIF›ENDPROC››' starts the title music from the beginning (called by every title screen)›PROC PlayMusic›  TEMPO 3›  ' voice 0: pure tone, volume 9, decay 4›  VOICE 0, 10, 9, 4›  ' voice 1: buzzy bass (distortion 12), volume 10, decay 6›  VOICE 1, 12, 10, 6›  ' voice 2: noise (distortion 8), volume 6, fast decay›  VOICE 2, 8, 6, 1›  MUSIC 0, LEAD›  MUSIC 1, BASS›  MUSIC 2, HATS›ENDPROC›